                <p class="mb-0">
                    Nested lists are created by placing a <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>
                    or <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code> inside a parent
                    <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>. They are useful for representing
                    hierarchical information such as course structures,
                    navigation menus, categories, roadmaps, and organizational
                    data. Different list types can be combined, and CSS can be
                    used to control indentation, spacing, and visual appearance.
